1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Nathan ben Ahija (Achaya) is the son of Ahija ((Achaya) David. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathan, went to Palestine, and by virtue of his ancestry gained a following among Palestinian Jews to displace the Hillelite "Nasi" Simon [Bar Gamaliel], but the conspiracy against the Palestinian Patriarch collapsed due to the fa
2 CONC ilure of the Palestinian Jews to rise up in his support. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was subsequently among the confidants of the patriarchal house, and in intimate relations with the Palestinian "Nasi" (135-165). His grandson, Rav[a], returned to the exilarchal house in Babylonia, AD 219, and died in AD 247.
