2 CONT For a description of the collections of gaonic responsa published through 1985 and studies on them, see Tsvi Groner, The Legal Methodology of Hai Gaon, Brown Judaic Studies 66 (Chico, Calif.: Scholars Press, 1985), pp. 173–187.
2 CONT
2 CONT A list of sixty works of responsa by rabbis of Spain and North Africa during the period of the rishonim can be found in Menachem Elon (ed.), Digest of the	 Responsa	 Literature of Spain and North Africa (Jerusalem: Hoṣaʾat ha-Makh
2 CONC on le-Ḥeqer ha-Mishpaṭ ha-ʿIvri and Magnes Press, 1981), pp. 30-33 [Hebrew].
2 CONT
2 CONT On the methods of historical use of the responsa literature, see also Haym Soloveitchik, Poland	 during the Sixteenth Century (Jerusalem: Hebrew University of Jerusalem, 1990) [Hebrew].
2 CONT
2 CONT The following list illustrates some of the more well known respondents and their printed editions in order to give a general sense of the breadth of the responsa literature:
2 CONT
2 CONT Naṭronai bar Hilai Gaʾon (d. 858, Iraq): The	 Responsa of Rav Na ṭ ronai bar Hilai Gaʾon: Published from Manuscripts and First Prints, ed. Robert Brody (Jerusalem: Makhon Ofeq, 1994), 562 responsa [Hebrew].
2 CONT
2 CONT Hai ben Sherira Gaʾon (d. 1038, Iraq): Tsvi Groner, “A List of Hai Gaon’s Responsa,” Alei Sefer 13 (1986). A bibliographical list of 1,112 responsa. [Hebrew].
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac ben Jacob Al-Fasi (d. 1103, Spain): (1) The Responsa of Rabbi Isaac Al-Fasi (Vienna: A. Shmid; 1794; repr. Jerusalem,  1974/75), 420 responsa [Hebrew]. (2) Responsa, ed. Zeʾev Byednovits (Biłgoraj: N. Ḳronenberg, 1935. repr.
2 CONC  Jerusalem: 1968/69), 176 responsa [Hebrew]. (3) The Responsa of Rabbi Isaac Al-Fasi, ed. Wolf Leiter (Pittsburgh: Makhon ha-Rambam, 1954), 419 responsa [Hebew]. (4) Sheʾelot u-Teshuvot be-Tosefet Ṣiyyunim, ed. Dov Ṣevi Roṭshṭeyn 
2 CONC (New York: Mekhon Ṣevi le-Moreshet Gedole Yisraʾel, 1974/75), 125 responsa [Hebrew].
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph ha-Levi ben Me’ir ibn Migash (d. 1114, Spain): The Responsa of	 Joseph ha-Levi ibn Migash, ed. Simḥa Ḥasida (Jerusalem: Mekhon Lev Sameaḥ,” 1990/91), 237 responsa [Hebrew].
2 CONT
2 CONT Moses Maimonides (d. 1204 Egypt): The	 Responsa	 of Maimonides: Published for the First Time in Their Original Arabic, ed. Joshua Blau (Jerusalem: Meḳitse Nirdamim, 1957–86), 481 responsa [Hebrew & Arabic].
2 CONT
