1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Scholars Dr. David Kelley and Dr Don Stone suspect that the name Zakai was introduced into this paternal line via the marriage of Yitzchak Avraham ben Nathan to a daughter of David ben Zakkai of Babylon.  David ben
2 CONC  Zakkai was the Rosh Golei of Babylon and Rosh Yeshiva of Sura.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Zakai ben Avraham had at least two (2) sons 1) David and 2) Abraham ben Nathan.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage among the Nagid HaGolah of al-Ifriqiya and Babylon Gaonim would bind Sura, Pumbeditha and Kairouan Mu'tazilite traditions.  This is a marriage between a Palestinian Exilarch and a Palestinian Exilarch's daughter.
