1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://he.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D7%A8%D7%9E%D7%91%22%D7%9F ]
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nahmanides  '''Nahmanides [Nah-man-nid-ez] (רבי משה בן נחמן), also known as Rabbi Moses ben Naḥman Girondi, Bonastruc ça (de) Porta and by his acronym Ramban (1194 – 1270), was a leading medieval Jewi
2 CONC sh scholar, Catalan Sephardic rabbi, philosopher, physician, kabbalist, and biblical commentator. He was raised, studied, and lived for most of his life in Girona, Catalonia.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Ramban was born in Girona in 1194, where he grew up and studied (hence his name "Girondi"), and died in the Land of Israel about 1270. He was the grandson of Isaac ben Reuben of Barcelona and cousin of Jonah Gerondi (the Rabbe
2 CONC inu Yonah); possibly his brother was Benveniste de Porta, the bailie of Barcelona. Among his teachers in Talmud were Judah ben Yakkar and Meïr ben Nathan of Trinquetaille, and he is said to have been instructed in Kabbalah (Jewish
2 CONC  mysticism) by his countryman Azriel of Gerona, who was in turn a disciple of Isaac the Blind.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nahmanides studied medicine which he practiced as a means of livelihood; he also studied philosophy. During his teens he began to get a reputation as a learned Jewish scholar. At age 16 he began his writings on Jewish law. In his 
2 CONC Milhamot Hashem (Wars of the Lord) he defended Alfasi's decisions against the criticisms of Zerachiah ha-Levi of Girona. These writings reveal a conservative tendency that distinguished his later works — an unbounded respect for t
2 CONC he earlier authorities.  [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nahmanides  ''biography continued]
2 CONT
2 CONT #[http://www.jewishvirtuallibrary.org/jsource/judaica/ejud_0002_0014_0_14480.html  Nahmanides]
2 CONT #[http://www.jewishencyclopedia.com/articles/11129-moses-ben-nahman-gerondi  Moses ben Nahman Gerondi]
2 CONT #[http://www3.nd.edu/~undpress/excerpts/P01210-ex.pdf  NAHMANIDES in Medieval Catalonia]
2 CONT #[http://www.girona.cat/call/eng/institut.php  Nahmanides Institute for Jewish Studies (scroll down to see list of personalities )
2 CONT
2 CONT #[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nahmanides  Nahmanides] Wikipedia
2 CONT # [http://jwa.org/encyclopedia/article/iggeret-ha-kodesh  Iggeret Ha-Kodesh]
2 CONT # Commentary on Torah, Genesis 1:1, Naḥmanides, quoted in Gerald Schroeder “Genesis and the Big Bang: The Discovery of Harmony Between modern Science and the Bible” ISBN 0-553-35413-2 p.65
2 CONT # p. 73 in Jonathan Sacks (2005) To Heal a Fractured World : The Ethics of Responsibility. London : Continuum (ISBN 9780826480392)
2 CONT # Caputo, Nina, Nahmanides in Medieval Catalonia: History, Community and Messianism. Notre Dame, IN: University of Notre Dame Press, 2008. Pp. 384.
2 CONT #[http://wiki.geni.com/index.php/Jewish_Dynasties  Jewish Dynasties]
2 CONT
2 CONT **************************************
2 CONT
2 CONT Please note that the JE article says: "... possibly his brother was Benveniste de Porta, the bailie of Barcelona." New evidence in the form of a will from 1268 CE demonstrates that Ramban WAS NOT THE BROTHER OF BENVENISTE DE PORTA
2 CONC . I have recommended that this connection be severed: see Discussion under https://www.geni.com/people/Perfet-Nasi/6000000017177766072
