1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Constanza Rodriguez de Maluenda appears as a daughter of Gonzalo Rodriguez de Maluenda in 1435 in https://www.fundacioncajacirculo.es/AHCB_D.php?cod=5842RR&nombre=Rodr%C3%ADguez,%20Constanza
2 CONT
2 CONT Contanza's second last name could also be Villena since in http://bibliotecadigital.rah.es/dgbrah/i18n/consulta/registro.cmd?id=45697  page 7 Luis de Salazar y Castro says that Gonzalo Rodriguez de Maluenda, son of Juan Garces de 
2 CONC Maluenda and Maria Nunez de Cartagena, "it is supposed" or "it was known" (the meaning of the words used can be interpreted differently) that he was married to a Maria de Villena.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the Maluenda "probanza de hidalguia" in page 248 of http://riubu.ubu.es/bitstream/10259.4/591/1/1133-9284_n097_p241-254.pdf it is said that Teresa Rodriguez de Maluenda was married to a Polanco. Teresa married Pedro Torquemada 
2 CONC and had many children with him according to Cantera Burgos so it is unlikely that it was her who married a Polanco and instead it was her sister.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is unclear if in this document of the Cathedral of Burgos, Gonzalo Lopez de Polanco appears as Gonzalo Perez de Polanco y Villena or if Villena is another person. https://www.fundacioncajacirculo.es/AHCB_D.php?cod=13968RR&nombr
2 CONC e=L%C3%B3pez%20de%20Polanco,%20Gonzalo
2 CONT
2 CONT Author Laura Lara Martinez in her book ''Ignacio y la Compañía: Del castillo a la misión'' (2015) claims that Constanza de Maluenda was the paternal greatgrandmother of the Jesuit Juan Alfonso de Polanco. For that to happen, Const
2 CONC anza needs to be the wife of Don Gonzalo Lopez Polanco (c.1420-?), his paternal greatgrandfather. https://books.google.se/books?id=2VwPCwAAQBAJ&pg=PT40&dq=juan+alfonso+polanco+maluenda&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwjgs_HoxsDZAhXCKCwKHYvXB
2 CONC rY4ChDoAQgrMAA#v=onepage&q=juan%20alfonso%20polanco%20maluenda&f=false
2 CONT
2 CONT https://books.google.se/books?id=db89AQAAIAAJ&q=polanco+astruch&dq=polanco+astruch&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwjilPiv18DZAhVBlSwKHRgBCbQQ6AEIKTAA
2 CONT
2 CONT Various authors claim the same thing as above, that Jesuit Juan Alfonso Polanco descends from the Maluenda family, again for that to happen, his paternal greatgrandmother needs to be a Rodriguez Maluenda born circa 1420-1430 https
2 CONC ://books.google.se/books?id=xCPtCwAAQBAJ&pg=PA191&dq=polanco+maluenda+converso&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwiQ9oq1m9nZAhVSyaQKHR76DiQQ6AEIKTAA#v=onepage&q=polanco%20maluenda%20converso&f=false
2 CONT
2 CONT Author Jose Garcia de Castro in his book "Polanco, el humanismo de los jesuitas" on page 13 also says that Juan Alfonso Polanco descends from the Maluendas (although he says its from his mother's side. His mother was Maria de Sali
2 CONC nas and there is no evidence that his maternal grandfather Juan Alonso de Salinas descends from the Maluendas and the genealogy of his maternal grandmother Catalina Iniguez de la Mota is an old Christian lineage. https://gcloyola.
2 CONC com/es/index.php?controller=attachment&id_attachment=101
2 CONT
2 CONT Maluenda lineage links-  https://sites.google.com/site/barbagen/maluenda http://bibliotecadigital.rah.es/dgbrah/i18n/consulta/registro.cmd?id=45697  page 7 (Descendants of Maria Nunez Ha-Levi)
2 CONT
2 CONT Cantera Burgos book on Alvar Garcia de Santa Maria descendants https://bibliotecadigital.jcyl.es/es/catalogo_imagenes/grupo.cmd?path=10067821
