2 CONT  David ibn Yaḥya Negro ben Gedaliah (ha-Rab shel Sefarad):
2 CONT
2 CONT A prominent figure during the war between the kings of Castile and Portugal. By divulging a secret he succeeded in frustrating the plot of Queen Leonora to murder her son-in-law, and as a reward he was appointed chief rabbi of Cas
2 CONC tile, while King João of Portugal disposed of his estates in that country. At the time of his death, which occurred at Toledo in Oct.; 1385, he held the post of "almoxarife" for King Ferdinand of Castile. His tombstone has been pr
2 CONC eserved. http://www.jewishencyclopedia.com/articles/15051-yahya#anchor6
