1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mother of Juan de Oñate, conquistador responsible for establishing Santa Fe, New Mexico
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Doña '''Catalina Salazar y de Cadeña''' born 1497 at Burgos, Spain died 1534
2 CONT
2 CONT Her grand-parents were members of the royal court of King Ferdinand and Queen Isabella of Spain.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her father was the lieutenant governor of all of New Spain and Factor of the Royal Treasuary in Mexico.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dona Catalina was married twice:
2 CONT
2 CONT #Don Ruy Diaz de Mendoza
2 CONT #Governor Cristóbal de Narriahondo Pérez de Oñate
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT
2 CONT ''With all Arms'' by Carl Laurence Duaine.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Don Juan de Onate Colonizer of New Mexico'' by George P. Hammond.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''The Last Conquistador, Juan de Onate and the settling of the far Southwest''.....the author, Marc Simmons, lists her 1st husband as Don Ruy Diaz de Mendoza.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Origen de los Fundadores de Texas, Nuevo Mexico, Coahuila, y Nuevo Leon, Saltillo Tomo II'' by Guillermo Garmendia Leal, page 66.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Glory, God, and Gold'' edited by Lewis Gannett.
