1 OCCU Alcalde de los Alcazeres Reales
1 TITL Alcalde del Alcazar
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Alcalde de los Reales Alcázares de Sevilla, seat of the Casa de la Contratacion de las Indias ("House of Trade) and center of the discoveries, explorations and colonization of the Kingdom of Spain. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the biggest financier, after the King, of the expedition of Sebastian Caboto in 1526 for a second circumnavigation of the World to the Molucca Islands in the Pacific, in order to find a shorter route to the Pacific than the
2 CONC  one established by the Magallanes expedition of 1520 and strengthen Spanish claims in the spice islands. This voyage was officially noted as an expedition for the discovery of Tarshish, Ophir, Eastern Cathay, and Cipango (Japan).
2 CONC  His son Alonso de Santa Cruz, Spain's most prominent cartographer and cosmographer in the House of Trade, also participated as an investor and supervisor of the expedition.
2 CONT
2 CONT When Caboto reached Brazil he found out about the riches of Rio de la Plata and abandoned the course of the expedition in search for wealth. This lead to the establishment of the first European settlement in present day Argentina 
2 CONC in 1527 called Sancti Spiritu.
2 CONT
