1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Gonzalez direct lines by Mary Anne Curray:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.currays.net/Gonzalez%20Web%20Project/ps05/ps05_416.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Esquibel, Jose Antonio, “Tragedy Among Onate’s Colony: A Chronicle of the Sosa Albornoz Family,” Nuestra Raices, Genealogical Society of Hispanic America, Spring 1998, Vol. 10, No. 1.
2 CONT
2 CONT p. 3:
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1540, they were residents of Santa Olalla, Spain, when their sons, don Francisco de Sosa Albornoz, a native of Toledo, Spain, and don Esteban de Sosa, came to Nueva Espana. 4 Don Francisco was successful in procuring matrimony 
2 CONC with dona Inez de Tapia y Sosa, daughter of the highly esteemed and remarkable conquistador Maese de Campo y Teniente don Andres de Tapia. Don Francisco and dona Inez became the parents of don Alonso de Sosa Albornoz, a native of 
2 CONC Mexico City born circa 1550, who eventually joined Onate’s colonizing expedition. 5
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.	Francisco SOSA ALBORNOZ m. 1560, Ines TAPIA SOSA, (daughter of Andres DE-TAPIA and Isabel DE-SOSA).
2 CONT * 1.	Alonso SOSA ALBORNOZ b. 1549, Xochitla, Mex, Mex, m. (1) abt 1565, Juana RAMIREZ ORTIZ, b. abt 1550, (daughter of Gabriel RAMIREZ and __________ ORTIZ) m. (2) 1585, Beatriz NAVARRO RODRIGUEZ, b. abt 1564, (daughter of Juan NA
2 CONC VARRO and Maria RODRIGUEZ SOSA). Alonso died abt 1601.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.vsalgs.org/stnemgenealogy/alonsoes.html
2 CONT
2 CONT ========================			
2 CONT
2 CONT Francisco de SOSA ALBORNOZ24,2980 was born (date unknown). A native of Toledo, Spain, he was one of the discoverers and conquerors of the new Kingdoms of Nueva Galicia and Nueva Viscaya in the new country of Nueva España. Parents:
2 CONC  Esteban de SOSA and Ana de ALBORNOZ. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Inez de TAPIA Sosa. Inez de TAPIA Sosa and Francisco de SOSA ALBORNOZ were married about 1560. Children were: Alonso de SOSA ALBORNOZ.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.raullongoria.net/Genealogy/FamilyTree/b214.html#P1723
2 CONT
2 CONT ==================================
2 CONT
2 CONT 20. FRANCISCO7 DE SOSA-GUEVARA-Y-ALBORNOZ (ESTEBAN6 DE SOSA-GUEVARA, JUAN-ALONSO5 DE ESTRADA, ANA4 ESTRADA-DE-LA-CABALLERIA, ALONSO3 DE ESTRADA, FERDINAND II (THE2 CATHOLIC), JOHN II OF1 ARAGON) was born 1530 in Santa Olalla, Spai
2 CONC n. He married INES DE TAPIA-Y-SOSA 1548 in Xochitla, Mexico City, D.F., Mexico, daughter of ANDRES DE TAPIA and ISABEL DE SOSA. She was born in Spain, and died in Mexico City, F.D., Mexico.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for FRANCISCO DE SOSA-GUEVARA-Y-ALBORNOZ:
2 CONT In the book, Mil Familias III, by Rodolfo Gonzalez de la Garza, he is listed as a descendent of the Don Alonso of Estrada, Duke of Aragon. Page 85. Conquistador of Nueva Galicia, Mexico.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage Notes for FRANCISCO DE SOSA-GUEVARA-Y-ALBORNOZ and INES DE TAPIA-Y-SOSA: Marriage source from the book, Mil Familias III by Rodolfo Gonzalez de la Garza. Page 85.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of FRANCISCO DE SOSA-GUEVARA-Y-ALBORNOZ and INES DE TAPIA-Y-SOSA are:
2 CONT * 28. i. CAPTAIN ALONSO8 DE SOSA-ALBORNOZ, b. Abt. 1549, Xochitle, Mexico F.D., Mexico; d. Abt. 1601, Murdered at San Gabriel, New Mexico.
2 CONT * ii. ANA DE SOSA-ALBORNOZ, d. Bef. 02 Sep 1591, Mexico City, F.D. Mexico?.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.somosprimos.com/inclan/estrada.htm
