1 NAME Conquistador Juan Navarro
1 NAME Juan /Navarro/ I
2 GIVN Juan
2 SURN Navarro
2 NSFX I
2 _MARNM Navarro
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE BEF 1507
2 ADDR
3 STAE Reino de Navarra
3 CTRY España
1 BAPM
2 DATE 9 MAR 1516
2 ADDR
3 CITY Santa Catalina
3 STAE Albacete
3 CTRY Spain
1 DEAT
2 DATE AFT 1575
2 ADDR
3 CTRY Reino de Nueva España
1 OCCU Conquistador, Participated in conquest of Mexico-Tenochtitlan
1 TITL Conquistador
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} García Pimentel, Luis, editor.  ''Relacion de los obispados de Tlaxcala, Michoacan, Oaxaca y otros lugares en el siglo XVI, Volume 5'', Editor's Home, Mexico City, Mexico, 1904,  page 160.  ...  https://books.googl
2 CONC e.com/books?id=TgYOAAAAIAAJ&pg=PA160&lpg=PA160&dq=Conquistador+juan+navarro&source=bl&ots=AaQN0aWQk1&sig=omEOcflJbfMpH3TbZQPc9oqAvII&hl=en&sa=X&ei=NarvVPWBKIyXNpTrgYgB&ved=0CDsQ6AEwBQ#v=onepage&q=Conquistador%20juan%20navarro&f=fa
2 CONC lse  ...  "''Cayanquilpa'', en el arzobispado de México, fué encomendado en '''Juan Navarro, conquistador''', primero tenedor, por cuya muerte sucedió en su mujer viuda, que después casó con Juan Bautista de Marin, y siendo viudo 
2 CONC de ella, casó segunda vez con Da. Leonor Marin, y él es difunto, la cual é sus hijas los poseen, sobre que el fiscal trata pleito."
2 CONT
2 CONT '''__________________________'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Feinberg, Benjamin.  ''The Devil's Book of Culture: History, Mushrooms, and Caves in Southern Mexico'', University of Texas Press, Austin, Texas, 2003, page 42.  ...  https://books.google.com/books?id=0asAAQAAQBAJ&pg=PA42&lpg=PA42
2 CONC &dq=Conquistador+juan+navarro&source=bl&ots=11-DhCRmvG&sig=Qt90hi247GEOhVakt4aiYqKVzks&hl=en&sa=X&ei=PrzvVIjjCsKXgwSrgYGIAg&ved=0CB0Q6AEwADgK#v=onepage&q=Conquistador%20juan%20navarro&f=false  ...  "The first territorial division 
2 CONC of 1536 left Huautla under the rule of Teotitlán, and the second division, in 1579, left the Sierra Mazateca, along with Teotitlán and La Cañada, as '''part of the encomienda of the conquistador Juan Navarro''' (Tibón 1983:45)."
2 CONT
2 CONT '''__________________________'''
2 CONT
2 CONT http://gw5.geneanet.org/sanchiz?lang=en;pz=tomas;nz=sanchez+garza;ocz=0;p=juan;n=navarro+navarra
2 CONT
2 CONT '''__________________________'''
2 CONT
2 CONT From the work of Miguel A Ayala (webcached 12/29/2012):
2 CONT
2 CONT http://webcache.googleusercontent.com/search?q=cache:http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/a/y/a/Miguel-A-Ayala-TX/WEBSITE-0001/UHP-0328.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Juan Navarro from Navarre, Spain, was of Basque descent. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He went to Santo Domingo in 1514; Cuba in 1519 and Mexico in 1520 with (Panfilo) Narvaez in order to arrest Cortez, and later joined Cortez (after Narvaez's defeat and capture). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Had a son Juan Navarro the younger born in 1533. The younger was one of the original settlers of San Martin, New Vizcaya (Durango, Mx) in 1556, where he put in the first ore-crushing mill. Also helped found Saltillo in 1577 and wa
2 CONC s married to Dona Maria Rodriguez.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''_______________________'''
2 CONT
