2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT His father was the very wealthy and financial backer of the entrada unto New Mexico. In 1599, during the second expedition into New Mexico, his father was the lieutenant governor and captain general of New Mexico. Source: From the
2 CONC  book, Don Juan de Oñate Colonizer of New Mexico, by George P. Hammond.
2 CONT
2 CONT On May 9, 1626, Don Vicente was the Maestro de Campo of Durango, Mexico. Mil Familias III, by Rodolfo Gonzalez de la Garza. Page 96.
2 CONT
2 CONT Origen de los Fundadores de Texas, Nuevo Mexico, Coahulia, y Nuevo Leon, by Guillermo Garmendia Leal. (page 49 & 156).
