1 NAME García /Pérez Polanco/
2 GIVN García
2 SURN Pérez Polanco
2 _MARNM Pérez Polanco
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1615
2 ADDR
3 CITY Santiago De Los Caballeros
3 CTRY Dominican Republic
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1656
2 PLAC Santiago, La Española
2 ADDR
1 TITL Capt.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Captain of the northern military bands defending the northern coast and towns against the buccaneers and the filibusters from the Tortuga Island
2 CONT
2 CONT Started his military career at 14 yrs old and was alferez of the military band of his father's cousin Capt. Antonio de Henao y Almeida going to the rescue of the city of Santo Domingo various times.
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://pares.mcu.es/ParesBusquedas20/catalogo/show/397774 "Méritos del Capitan y Sargento Mayor Don Pedro Perez Polanco. Carta del Gobernador Francisco Segura Sandoval y Castilla (1680)". Archivo General de Indias, Santo_Domingo,
2 CONC  64,R.2,N.39.] Image no. 149
2 CONT
2 CONT He was also alcalde de la Santa Hermandad and alcalde ordinario of the city of Santiago de los Caballeros
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://pares.mcu.es/ParesBusquedas20/catalogo/show/397774 "Méritos del Capitan y Sargento Mayor Don Pedro Perez Polanco. Carta del Gobernador Francisco Segura Sandoval y Castilla (1680)". Archivo General de Indias, Santo_Domingo,
2 CONC  64,R.2,N.39.] Image no. 162
2 CONT
2 CONT By 1647, Capitan Garcia Perez Polanco had hatos in La Vega according to a story from the book "La Mala Vida ..." by Carlos Esteban Deive page 82-83 (attached in media section)
2 CONT
2 CONT Torres Agudo, Ruth. "Los Campuzano-Polanco, una familia de la élite de la ciudad de Santo Domingo". Nuevo Mundo Mundos Nuevos [online]
