1 NOTE {geni:about_me} At Santa Fe on 10 October 1661, Francisco de Madrid II, father of Roque de Madrid, was Comisario de Cavallos and gave his age as forty-seven, more or less, indicating he was born circa 1614.
2 CONT
2 CONT In October 1661, the wife of Francisco de Madrid was named as doña María de Albizu (born circa 1621) who was described as a daughter of Maese de Campo don Tomás de Albizu (ONMF: 2). Doña María’s first husband was Cristóbal Enríque
2 CONC z (see Enríquez) who was referred to in the testimony of Capitán Tomás de la Huerte (age thirty-two; 29 October 1661) as "fulano Enriques."
