1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Served for thirteen years in Naples, Milan and Flanders as lieutenant of Infantry (where he was found at the site of Ostend and on the relief of the Antwerp dyke), then went to the Regiment of the Count-Duke, in wh
2 CONC ich he graduated as captain
2 CONT
2 CONT Juan de Salamanca entered as a soldier in 1625 in the Royal Navy of the Ocean Sea, in the company of Nicolás Giudice, in which he was on board ("being named for the boarding") until 1629. He attended, among other actions, the "Rel
2 CONC ief of Cádiz "in 1625 against the English (action immortalized by Zurbarán in a painting for the Salón de Reinos del Buen Retiro). He later went ashore, married and had his children. In 1632 he obtained mercy habit of the Order of
2 CONC  Calatrava. In 1639, destined in the Four Villas of the Coast of the Sea (Santander, Laredo, Castro Urdiales and San Vicente de la Barquera), was in the defense of Colindres (Cantabria) against the entrance of the French Army unde
2 CONC r the command of the Archbishop of Bordeaux
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1657 he was appointed governor and captain general of Cuba to replace Diego Rangel
2 CONT
2 CONT http://dbe.rah.es/biografias/26098/juan-de-salamanca-y-salamanca
