1 NAME Pedro /Pérez Polanco/
2 GIVN Pedro
2 _MARNM Pérez Polanco
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Convent of the Dominican Order
2 ADDR
3 CITY Santo Domingo
3 CTRY Dominican Republic
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1635
2 ADDR
3 CITY Santiago De Los Caballeros
3 CTRY Dominican Republic
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1714
2 ADDR
3 CITY Santo Domingo
3 CTRY Dominican Republic
1 TITL Captain
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mayor of Santiago de los Caballeros from 1661-1666, a title that was acquired for him by his grandfather don Pedro Polanco de Henao, who was Alguacil Mayor of La Vega and later of Santiago between 1620-1660
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://pares.mcu.es/ParesBusquedas20/catalogo/show/406560 Confirmacion de Oficio Pedro Perez Polanco 1661 SANTO_DOMINGO,903a Images 183-187]
2 CONT
2 CONT Utrera, Fray Cipriano de (1979). Noticias históricas de Santo Domingo, Volume 3. Santo Domingo: Editora Taller. pp. 72, 324. (Attached in media section)
2 CONT
2 CONT He was also twice alcalde ordinario of Santiago and Captain of Infantry for more than 10 years before becoming Mayor Sergeant 
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://pares.mcu.es/ParesBusquedas20/catalogo/show/397774 "Méritos del Capitan y Sargento Mayor Don Pedro Perez Polanco. Carta del Gobernador Francisco Segura Sandoval y Castilla (1680)". Archivo General de Indias, Santo_Domingo,
2 CONC  64,R.2,N.39. pp. Image no. 72.] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He has been Governador de Armas of Santiago for the same period of time and has been to the rescue of the city of Santo Domingo with his "compania" (military band) numerous times.
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://pares.mcu.es/ParesBusquedas20/catalogo/show/397774 "Méritos del Capitan y Sargento Mayor Don Pedro Perez Polanco. Carta del Gobernador Francisco Segura Sandoval y Castilla (1680)". Archivo General de Indias, Santo_Domingo,
2 CONC  64,R.2,N.39. pp. Image no. 76.] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was also mayordomo and deputy of the Cofradia del Santisimo Sacramento [http://pares.mcu.es/ParesBusquedas20/catalogo/show/397774 "Méritos del Capitan y Sargento Mayor Don Pedro Perez Polanco. Carta del Gobernador Francisco Seg
2 CONC ura Sandoval y Castilla (1680)". Archivo General de Indias, Santo_Domingo, 64,R.2,N.39. pp. Image no. 82. and 114] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the owner of the Hato of Bonagua in La Vega which he had inherited from his grandfather Pedro Polanco de Henao as his only grandson and sucessor. [https://books.google.se/books?id=zzjwG6q7FecC&pg=PA58&dq=Polanco+Buenagua+La
2 CONC +espa%C3%B1ola:+anotaciones+hist%C3%B3ricas&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwigyY6gpMfcAhVJ2SwKHWY1BQgQ6AEIKTAA#v=onepage&q=Polanco%20Buenagua%20La%20espa%C3%B1ola%3A%20anotaciones%20hist%C3%B3ricas&f=false Gil-Bermejo García, Juana. "La esp
2 CONC añola: anotaciones históricas, 1600-1650 (p. 58-60)"]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1677 Capt Pedro Perez Polanco and Capt. Pedro Morel de Santa Cruz, along with other captains, led the "Desalojo de Samana" or the eviction of the enemies from the Samana bay. "Samana y su porvenir" P.55 (attached in the media s
2 CONC ection)
2 CONT
2 CONT Grandfather of the Campuzano Polanco brothers
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Campuzano_Polanco_family
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
