1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Bishop Hans Lehman b. ca. 1702, Canton Bern, Switzerland. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1727 Hans & Anna sailed with 3 children from Rotterdam, Holland aboard ship James Goodwill and landed in Philadelphia, PA.They settled in Rapho Township, Lancaster County, PA. Hans bought 197 acres of land northwest of Manheim,
2 CONC  between present day Colebrook Street and Hernley. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans was a minister & bishop in Hernley Mennonite Church. This cemetery, where three generations of Lehmans are buried, has since been obliterated and the tombstones laid down so it can be plowed over.(Daniel R. Lehman, genealogis
2 CONC t and researcher, correspondence with Ruth Runion-Slear, 2007)(Lehman, Daniel R."Bishop Hans Lehman, Immigrant of 1727" Pennsylvania Mennonite Heritage, October 1980, pp. 16-23) [https://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&a
2 CONC mp;GRid=110549325&amp;ref=acom Find a Grave]
2 CONT
