1 OCCU Av Bais Din in Dubno, Av Beis Din of Roizna and Dubna, A.B.D. Dubno, AB"D Dubno
1 TITL Rabbi
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Av Beit Din of Rovno and later Av Beit Din of Dubno.  In the 1903 Jewish Encyclopedia, Volume 5, Page 6 he is listed as Eleazar b. Issachar Baer of Cracow.  He was the Rabbi of Cracow from 1714 to 1719.  Maternal g
2 CONC randfather of Ezekiel Landau.  Immediately following him as Rabbi is listed "Heschel  Eleazar (also called Heschel "der Kleiner") died July 25, 1729.
2 CONT
2 CONT Among the chief rabbis of Dubno was R. Eleazar, A.B.D. Rovno and later A.B.D. Dubno, son of R. Issachar Berish of Cracow, son of R. Heschel of Cracow. In the 1903 Jewish Encyclopedia, vol. V, p.6 he is listed as "Eleazar b. Issach
2 CONC ar Baer of Cracow (1714-1719), maternal grandfather of Ezekiel Landau." Immediately following him as rabbi is listed "Heschel b. Eleazar (also called Heschel "der Kleiner"), died July 25, 1729."
2 CONT
2 CONT A more recently published work on the life, family and works of R. Heschel, Chanukat HaTorah HeChadash, by Shimon Schlesser, Bnai Brak, 1996, p.35 correctly records the children of R. Heschel and that Eleazar was a grandson. Furth
2 CONC er, in 1989, R. Samuel David Movshovitz, Jerusalem, in Chidushei Rabeinu Jacob MiLublin veRabeinu Heschel miKrakow, footnotes on page 19 in the introduction (#24) the reference to Da'at Kedoshim, but does not record Eleazar as one
2 CONC  of the sons. 
2 CONT
2 CONT R' ELEAZAR OF DUBNO - HE WAS THE AV BAIS DIN IN DUBNO. HE WAS THE GRANDSON OF R' ABRAHAM YEHOSHUA HESCHEL OF CRACOW. R' ELEAZAR WAS THE MATERNAL GRANDFATHER OF THE NODA B'YEHUDA
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Discussion on error in some sources
2 CONT Source: "The Unbroken Chain", by Dr. Neil Rosenstein, Volume 2, Page 715 
2 CONT
2 CONT There is a detailed discussion in a commentary '''LeDor VaDor''', by R. Naftali Braunfeld, appended to R. Jekutiel Aryey Kamelhar's '''Dor Deah''', New York, 1953 (p.4-5 end).  Here Bruanfeld shows how numerous old sources are in 
2 CONC error by making Eliezer, A.B.D. Dubno, son of Heschel and not the son of Issachar Berish, son of Heschel.
2 CONT
2 CONT He further shows that it was Eliezer's daughter, Chaya, who married Judah Landau (father of Ezekiel, Noda BiYehuda) and not the oft repeated error that Chaya  married Judah's father, Zvi Hirsch Landau.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kamelhar in M.H.D. agrees with Braunfeld's conclusion.  However Braunfeld does not raise the question of possibility that there was both a son of Heschel and a grandson of Heschel with the same name, and could even have both been 
2 CONC A.B.D. Dubno, although older sources could have become confused.
2 CONT
2 CONT For this reason both Eliezer's are being preserved in this book.  See the Landau Family Pedigree.  R. Joseph Lewinstein in HaEshkol, volt, p.188-9 does not include Eliezer as a son.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Possible error:
2 CONT
2 CONT From Geni.com:
2 CONT
2 CONT Av Beit Din of Rovno and later Av Beit Din of Dubno.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 1903 Jewish Encyclopedia, he is listed as Eleazar b. Issachar Baer of Cracow (1714-1719). Rabbi of Cracow from 1714 to 1719. Maternal grandfather of Ezekiel Landau. Heschel Eleazar (also called Heschel "der Kleiner") immedi
2 CONC ately followed him as Rabbi. Died July 25, 1729.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Among the chief rabbis of Dubno was R. Eleazar, A.B.D. Rovno and later A.B.D. Dubno, son of R. Issachar Berish of Cracow, son of R. Heschel of Cracow.
2 CONT
2 CONT A more recently published work on the life, family and works of R. Heschel, Chanukat HaTorah HeChadash, by Shimon Schlesser, Bnai Brak, 1996, p.35 correctly records the children of R. Heschel and states that Eleazar was a grandson
2 CONC . Further, in 1989, R. Samuel David Movshovitz, Jerusalem, in Chidushei Rabeinu Jacob MiLublin veRabeinu Heschel miKrakow, footnotes on page 19 in the introduction (#24) there is reference to Da'at Kedoshim, but Eleazar is not rec
2 CONC orded as one of the sons.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT R' Eleazar of Dubno - Av Bet Din of Dubno and grandson of R' Abraham Yehoshua Heschl of Cracow.  R' Eleazar was the maternal grandfather of the Noda b' Judah.
2 CONT
2 CONT Discussion of an error in some sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: "The Unbroken Chain", by Dr. Neil Rosenstein, Volume 2, Page 715:
2 CONT
2 CONT There is a detailed discussion in a commentary LeDor VaDor, by R. Naftali Braunfeld, appended to R. Jekutiel Aryey Kamelhar's Dor Deah, New York, 1953 (p.4-5 end). Here Bruanfeld shows how numerous old sources are in error by maki
2 CONC ng Eliezer, A.B.D. Dubno, son of Heschel and not the son of Issachar Berish, son of Heschel.
2 CONT
2 CONT He further shows that it was Eliezer's daughter, Chaya, who married Judah Landau (father of Ezekiel, the Noda BiYehuda) and not the oft repeated error that Chaya married Judah's father, Zvi Hirsch Landau.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kamelhar in M.H.D. agrees with Braunfeld's conclusion. However Braunfeld does not raise the question of possibility that there was both a son of Heschel and a grandson of Heschel with the same name, and could even have both been A
2 CONC .B.D. Dubno, although older sources could have become confused.
2 CONT
2 CONT For this reason both Eliezers are being preserved in this book. See the Landau Family Pedigree. R. Joseph Lewinstein in HaEshkol, volt, p.188-9 does not include Eliezer as a son.
