2 CONC quently he was elected Rabbi of Rzesz'ow from 1724-1728. In 1728 he was appointed as Rabbi of both the towns of Glogau and Lviv, a position held until 1740. In 1740 he was appointed Rabbi of Amsterdam (a position that was offered 
2 CONC to his father Saul years earlier), a position he held until his death in 1755. A call was extended to him from Prague in 1751, but he did not accept it. While the Jewish Encyclopedia is doubtful of whether he was rabbi in Lviv, as
2 CONC  stated by Buber (Anshe Shem, p. 38), Dembitzer in the Klilat Yofi and Reuven Margaliot provide proof of his position in Lviv/Lemberg, with Dembitzer stating that he held both positions simultaneously, while Margaliot is of the op
2 CONC inion that he changed positions a number of times in those years between the rabbinate of Glogau and Lviv.
2 CONT
2 CONT Works
2 CONT
2 CONT Aryeh did not publish any books, and what there is of his exists in the works of others-as in the responsa of Ẓebi Ashkenazi, No. 76; in those of Mordecai of D'fcsseldorf (Maamar Mordecai, Nos. 62, 63, Br'fcnn, 1790), and in the w
2 CONC orks of his son Saul, Binyan Ariel (Amsterdam, 1778)-and shows no originality. He took an active part in the controversy between Jacob Emden and Jonathan Eybesch'fctz, and sided with the former, who was his wife's brother. His let
2 CONC ters on that controversy are full of invectives against Eybesch'fctz (see Emden's Sefat Emet, p. 16, Lemberg, 1877). According to the testimony of his brother-in-law, Jacob Emden (see the latter's autobiography, Megillat Sefer, pp
2 CONC . 21, 68, Warsaw, 1896), he was a man of mediocre abilities, whose scientific attainments were not above the practical requirements for the rabbinical office.
2 CONT
2 CONT Descendants
2 CONT
2 CONT Of his sons, one, Saul Aryeh, was his successor, while the other, who called himself Hirschel Lewin or Levin, was Chief rabbi in London and Berlin. The son of the latter was Chief rabbi Solomon Herschell, first Chief Rabbi of the 
2 CONC British Empire. Saul's daughter Sarah Leah was the wife of Yitzhak HaLevi, the rabbi of Krak'f3w from 1776 till his death in 1799. Yitzhak HaLevi's son Tzvi Hirsch David Ha-Levi was Acting Rabbi of Krak'f3w from 1799 and formally 
2 CONC appointed Rabbi of Krak'f3w in 1816 till his death in 1831.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From Geni.com:
2 CONT
2 CONT LEIB Fishles Der Hoicher (The Tall) and Yuta's daughter Ester married Shaul Löwenstamm son of Abraham Yehoshua Heschel (1596-1663).
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Chacham Zvi Ashkenazi
2 CONT
2 CONT They had a son Aryeh LEIB (1690-1756) who married Miriam ASHKENAZI the daughter of the Chacham Zvi ASHKENAZI and his wife Sara MIRLES.
2 CONT
2 CONT See the 1700 painting of the Chacham Zvi. One copy of this painting is in the Jewish Mueseum in London. Another copy is in Jerusalem at Josh BUSH's father's cousin's house. A third copy is in the possession of a family in London, 
2 CONC a relative of Paul SHAVIV. There is a great story around this painting. It is probably the very first time that a Rabbi was actually painted. Since than, it became more acceptable. One story is that the Chacham Zvi was interviewin
2 CONC g for a rabbinical position in London. Another story is that he was called to London to settle a dispute amoung the Sephardim - possibly to check a controversial sermon preached by Chacham David Nieto for heresy. In any case, the 
2 CONC door was left open a bit and seemingly, without his knowledge the painter painted him.
2 CONT
2 CONT His son Yakov Emden (The YaBetz: Yakov Ben Zvi) writes about it in his very famous biography entitled Megilat Sefer.) A slightly different portrait of the Hakham Tzvi appears in M. H. GANS, Memorbook, Baarn, 1977, p. 163, together
2 CONC  with the more famous copy in London.
2 CONT
2 CONT Zvi Hersch Berlin (Rabbi Hart Lion) The son of Arie LEIB and Miriam was Zvi Hersch Berlin (Rabbi Hart Lion)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
