1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://barkai-family.com/Documents/Family%20Tree%201.jpg
2 CONT
2 CONT -------
2 CONT
2 CONT né vers 1655? (GenAmi)
2 CONT
2 CONT Dessau in 1696
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Howard Lesser : I have him born most likely in 1642 in Hamburg and settling later on in Dessau. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ______________
2 CONT
2 CONT Saul Wahl was named after his great grandfather, R' Saul Wahl and thus was born sometime after 1620.
2 CONT
2 CONT He went to Dessau in his latter years (1682 circa) and died there on July 5th 1717, about one hundred years after his namesake
2 CONT
2 CONT At this time, Dessau was the chief town of the German Duchy of Anhalt.
2 CONT
2 CONT About the time of Saul's arrival there were only about 26 Jewish families. Among them was R' Moses (Berend) Benjamin Wulff (called the "Tall Jew"), who was Saul's first cousin and a Court Jew in Dessau where he had settled in 1620
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT Details of these interrelationships can be found in the Ms.AR-A42 114 (Itzig), Leo Beck Institute, New York:
2 CONT
2 CONT *   The Mendelssohns, Alexander Altmann (University of Alabama Press, 1973).
2 CONT
2 CONT *   For the Mendelssohn lineage see also the periodical Genologie Vol 8, 16. Jahrgang, Heft 3 March 1967 pp 644-55.
2 CONT
2 CONT *   Max Freudenthal in his Aus der Heimat Moses Mendelssohns (Berlin 1900) mentions that the Dessau Jewish cemetry he found the grave of Saul Wahl, Moses' grandfather, which states that he was a descendant of Saul Wahl the king.
2 CONT
2 CONT *   A picture of this tombstone can be found in the Jewish Encyclopaedia (New York 1903) Vol 1v p. 535.
2 CONT
2 CONT *   See also Gerhard Ballin, Musikgeschichte und Genealofie X, the Ancestry of the composer Felix Mendelssohn Bartholdy p 644 ff.
2 CONT
2 CONT It seems most likely that Saul went to Dessau because of his cousins, who had found a life more satisfactory in the German Duchy.s R' Moses established a Beth HaMidrash there which was headed by R' Benjamin Wolf.
2 CONT
2 CONT Saul Wahl married Sisa (Susanna) died in 1730, the daughter of R' Menachem Man of Kalisc.
2 CONT
2 CONT Through the intercession of the Wulffs, Saul received permission from the Duke Johann George of Dessau to open the first brandy factory in 1696.  Records also mention Saul and Sisa Wahl as visitors to the popular annual event in t
2 CONC he nearby city - the Leipzig Fair. About 750 Jews used to attend the fair in its early years, and were involved in the buying and selling the many goods on display.  They were even permitted to have their own rooms for prayer Jude
2 CONC nschulen, so that by the year of Saul's death, there were separate rooms fo each of the Jewish groups from Berlin, Dessau, Halberstadt, Hamburg and Prague.
