1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Isaac/Yitshak Levy of Hatten, husband of Dinna. They appear together in the 1784 Hatten Jewish census (GG 68/51, household 9). His gravestone in the Jewish cemetery of Haguenau (section 15, F67HAG-1713) names his f
2 CONC ather as Shimshon, describes Isaac as סג״ל (Segal/Levite) of Hatten, and records his death and burial on 5 October 1789. Civil records for sons Moïse and Joachim identify their parents as Isaac and Dina; the family’s change from L
2 CONC evi to Weil is documented in Moïse’s 1808 name declaration. Source: original grave photograph and transcription supplied by the Service Musée-Archives de Haguenau, 11 August 2026, together with the cited census and civil registers
2 CONC .
