1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Domingo Martín Serran was married to Josefa de Herrera. A witness in 1694, he declared he was born in Santa Fé, giving his age as forty-seven in that year, and a eighty in 1726. He died at the age of ninety on Febr
2 CONC uary, 27 1735.
2 CONT
2 CONT His known children are Diego, who married Pascuala de Soto at Santa Cruz in 1694; María, wife of Juan Luján; Blas, who married Rosa de Vargas Machuca in 1705; and Matías, hasband of Josefa Luján Domínguez.
2 CONT
2 CONT ONMF, pg. 222
2 CONT
2 CONT He escaped the Pueblo Revolt of 1680, and returned to New Mexico with his family in 1693 as part of the Diego de Vargas group of settlers.
2 CONT
2 CONT Census: El Paso Area Muster, Dec 1692-Jan 1693, Pueblo la Ysleta del Sur, Nuevo Méjico. Nueva España. 287
2 CONT
2 CONT Fourth household, four sons, four daughters
2 CONT
2 CONT Domingo Martín, married to Josefa Herrera, with eight children, named Diego, age twenty-two, Matías, sixteen; Miguel, nine; Blas, six; Sebastiana, thirteen; María, twelve; Juana, fourt; and Bárbar, nuring; and his mother-in-law, n
2 CONC amed Juana de los Reyes. He states that, as his majesty's loyal vassal, he will go to settle with his family, if there is provisioning for it.
2 CONT
2 CONT Royal Crown Restored, pg. 60
